course: dictionary
lesson: 3137
title: Same word, different animal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words mean different things in different places. Elk is one of them. In Britain and Europe, an elk is the largest kind of deer, with huge flat antlers and a long face. «The moose, called elk in Britain, is the largest deer.» The sentence tells you the animal has two names, and the names depend on where you are.
explain: In North America, the word elk means a different animal: a large deer with branching antlers, also called a wapiti, and smaller than a moose. «The elk, called a moose in America, is the biggest deer in the world.» The same word, two different animals. This is a trap, so always check the clues in the sentence.
explain: Context also shows you what a word does in a text. «Wolves eat elk, elk eat trees, and trees shade streams.» Here elk are animals that eat plants. Ask yourself: where is this text set, and what is the animal doing? The clues will tell you which elk the writer means.
fact: Elk means a large deer, but which deer depends on the country.
fact: In Britain and Europe, elk means the animal called a moose in North America.
fact: In North America, elk means a large deer with branching antlers, also called a wapiti.
fact: «Antlers» are the bony growths on a deer's head, and males grow them and drop them each year.
fact: When a word changes meaning between countries, the context and the country of the text are your best clues.
exercise: «The moose, called elk in Britain, is the largest deer.» In Britain, what is this animal called? | Willow | *Elk | Wapiti | Beaver
exercise: In North America, what does elk mean? | The largest deer, with huge flat antlers and a long face | A kind of tree that grows by rivers | *A large deer with branching antlers, smaller than a moose | A type of wolf
exercise: «Wolves eat elk, elk eat trees, and trees shade streams.» What are the elk in this sentence? | Fish that swim upstream | Wolves that hunt in packs | Trees that grow near streams | *Plant-eating animals
test: «The elk, called a moose in America, is the biggest deer in the world.» Which animal is the elk here? | *The biggest deer, with huge flat antlers | A tree that grows near rivers | A smaller deer with branching antlers, the wapiti | A grey wolf
test: Why might a road sign in Canada warn drivers about elk? | Elk dig holes in the road at night | Elk sell petrol at the roadside | *Large deer might run onto the road | Elk are tiny birds that fly low over the road
exam: «Elk» means different animals in different countries; which is the best way to work out which one a text means? | *Check the country and the clues in the sentences | Skip the word and never come back to it | Ignore the word because it is too hard | Guess the first animal that comes into your head
